    "title": "NICU babies are in the Christmas spirit decked out in festive costumes at UNC Health - NewsBreak",
    "text": "17 minutes ago\nIn light of the Christmas season, the babies at UNC Health Rex's Neonatal Intensive Care Unit (NICU) were dressed in Christmas costumes.\nNurses dressed the little ones in Christmas costumes like Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer, gingerbread, a snowman, a Christmas tree, Santa Claus, and more.\nThe adorable costumes were a way to lift parents' spirits, since they will spend the holiday at the hospital with their babies.\nPremature infants can spend days, weeks and sometimes months in the NICU.\nSEE ALSO | Mom shares warning about batteries in Christmas gifts after daughter's injury",
